{"id": "EUVD-2026-97653", "enisaUuid": "d73df7a0-fea0-3317-879b-f867408a3b97", "description": "Gitoxide gix-pack before 0.75.0 contains an uncontrolled memory allocation vulnerability that allows remote attackers to abort the process by supplying a huge pack-header object count. Malicious remotes can serve a 12-byte pack header claiming 0xFFFFFFFF objects, forcing Tree::with_capacity to reserve hundreds of gigabytes and crash clone or fetch operations.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-12T16:05:33", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/GitoxideLabs/gitoxide/security/advisories/GHSA-x862-c2wj-4mwr", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitoxide-gix-pack-before-0.75.0-denial-of-service-via-pack-header-object-count"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109351", "GHSA-hf39-hrp5-hx3v"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "92bfd90a-45c5-3794-8c2e-0fc3c3a6edcb", "product": {"name": "gix-pack", "vendor": {"name": "GitoxideLabs"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.75.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a74f26f3-c818-3e98-9da4-4034fc3bacb8", "vendor": {"name": "GitoxideLabs"}}], "isExploited": false}